      "pins": ["U3.1", "U3.4", "A1.2", "C18.1", "U2.22", "R3.1"],
      "nets": ["NFC_INT"],
      "observed": "The net NFC_INT contains U3 pin 1 (LA), A1 pin 2 (B), and C18 pin 1, in addition to the intended U3 pin 4 (FD), U2 pin 22 (PA6), and R3 pin 1.",
      "expected": "NFC_INT should only connect U2 pin 22 (PA6), R3, and U3 pin 4 (FD). The antenna LA terminal (U3 pin 1), A1 pin 2, and C18 pin 1 should be on a separate antenna net, not tied to the field-detect signal.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"5\") (name \"NFC_INT\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"A1\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"B\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"C18\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"R3\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"22\") (pinfunction \"PA6\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"LA\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"FD\") (pintype \"output\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "NFC_INT net: U2 pin 22 (PA6) — R3 (10 kΩ) to VCC — U3 pin 4 (FD)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The NFC antenna coil is shorted to the field-detect output and MCU pin, detuning the antenna and corrupting the FD signal, likely preventing NFC communication.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain a bridged-net anomaly: the NFC_INT net incorrectly merges the NFC antenna LA terminal (U3.1, A1.2, C18.1) with the field-detect signal (U3.4, U2.22, R3.1), which would break NFC operation."
}

